# Server message i18n

**Strategy:** Server resolves locale at request time; API returns **one localized string** per user-facing field. UI displays it **as-is** — do not run server `Message`/`Title` through `t()`.

**Locales:** `en`, `hi` — align with `@saas-builder/i18n-contract` (`SUPPORTED_LOCALES`). Normalize BCP-47 to primary subtag (`en-IN` → `en`).

## Locale resolution (server)

Precedence: **`Accept-Language`** (active app/header locale) → authenticated **`PreferredLocale`** (JWT/profile) → **`en`**.

Reference: `NotificationRuleCatalog.normalizeLocale` in `backend-hospital`.

## Message-bearing fields

Localize any field intended for end-user display:

- Envelope: `Message` in `StandardApiResponse` / `ApiResponse`
- Domain: `Title`, `Message`, `Description`, `Body`, email/SMS/push templates
- Validation summaries in envelope `Message`
- FastAPI response `Message` fields in `ai-service`

**Never localize:** `ErrorCode`, enum/status codes, log strings, internal exception class names.

## Storage patterns

| Pattern | When | How |
|---------|------|-----|
| **Static bundles** | Fixed operational copy (errors, validation, success toasts) | Spring `messages_en.properties` / `messages_hi.properties`; resolve in shared `MessageResolver` or `@RestControllerAdvice`. FastAPI: equivalent locale bundles. |
| **DB per-locale rows** | Admin-editable or templated domain copy | One row per supported locale; fallback to `en`. Reference: `notification_event_rule_messages`. |

Pick one pattern per entity. **Never** hardcode English in controllers/services for user-facing text.

## Wire format

- One resolved string per field (not a `{ en, hi }` map on the wire)
- PascalCase wire keys (`api-json-pascal-case.mdc`)
- Errors: always include stable `ErrorCode` + localized `Message`

```json
{ "Success": false, "Message": "अमान्य ईमेल या पासवर्ड", "ErrorCode": "AUTH_INVALID_CREDENTIALS" }
```

## Client contract

- Set **`Accept-Language`** on every API request to the active app locale (`apiClient.ts`, mobile `client.ts`)
- Display envelope `Message` and domain `Title`/`Message` **as returned** — server owns the text
- Do **not** build `ErrorCode → i18n` registries for standard API errors
- Exception: transport/technical codes (timeouts, stream internals) may map to client keys in `httpUserFacingErrors.ts`
- UI metadata `i18nBundles` is **client chrome copy only** — not API errors (`extensibility.mdc`)

## Forbidden

```java
// ❌ Hardcoded English in controller
StandardApiResponse.error("Invalid email or password", "AUTH_INVALID_CREDENTIALS");

// ✅ Resolve via message bundle
StandardApiResponse.error(messages.get("error.auth.invalid_credentials", locale), "AUTH_INVALID_CREDENTIALS");
```

```typescript
// ❌ Re-translate server Message
toastStore.show(t(`errors.${errorCode}`), 'error');

// ✅ Show server-localized Message
toastStore.show(pickString(payload, ['Message']), 'error');
```

- Throwing `IllegalArgumentException("English text")` that leaks via `ex.getMessage()` to clients
- Localizing `ErrorCode` values
- Mixing `i18nBundles` with API error bundles

**Legacy:** Existing English-only endpoints should be migrated when touched. Reference impl: `NotificationRuleCatalog` + `NotificationService`.
